{"duration_api_ms":244633,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c49fbe17-b75f-4a38-b471-2868ef9bd887","total_cost_usd":0.290676,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12488,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24072,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17607},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12488,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":24072,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12488,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12488},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":24072,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12488,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.290676,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":17607,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"None of the 20 evaluated designs is feasible, and 10 returned no geometry. The geometry failures all occur where nose-sphere and shoulder overlap: a fit to the 10 failures and to valid rows gives a rough validity rule of 2*bluntness*cos(cone_half_angle) below about 0.92 (valid up to 0.919, invalid from 0.983). The max_g limit is 12 (implied by the margins). It rises with steeper flight path angle and is about 10-11.6 g at gamma of -1.5 to -3.2. The bondline limit is 450 K. Heatshield mass fraction grows roughly with D^2 and with cone length, so D is capped near 3.2-3.3 m for cone angles above 55 deg, and lower for low cone angles. Large D lowers both objectives. Peak flux follows roughly q ~ 6.5e6*sqrt(sin|gamma|/(bluntness*D^3)). Bondline rise (T-300) falls with steeper gamma and rises with flux.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-e948676086c1 (D 4.12, b 0.32, gamma -3.2) has 341 kW/m2, 403 K and 11.6 g. Only the mass fraction fails (-1.145), so shrinking D toward 3.1-3.3 should make it feasible.\",\"C-ddca85038195 (D 2.68, gamma -4.34) has 12.9 g against the 12 g limit, while C-b9d89f4e803a (gamma -1.93) has 9.9 g and C-e948676086c1 (gamma -3.2) has 11.6 g. This puts the g boundary near gamma of -3.5.\",\"C-f9dc, C-66547069c09c and C-af897bb220d2 have D of 3.7-4.2 m and mass-fraction margins of -0.31, -0.33 and -1.41. C-ddca85038195 (D 2.68) has margin +0.35 and C-62b9c4fe3119 (D 2.14) has +0.58. The mass limit is therefore D of about 3.2-3.3 m at high cone angle.\",\"C-b9d89f4e803a (-1.93 deg, 494 K) and C-23922e95d112 (-1.56 deg, 574 K) are both over the 450 K bondline limit with small D, so shallow entry with small D drives bondline temperature up. C-66547069c09c (-7.9 deg, 362 K) and C-e948676086c1 (-3.2 deg, 403 K) at similar flux show steeper entry gives a cooler bondline.\",\"Geometry failures such as C-90b619cf2774 (b 1.29, cone 53.7), C-5d0e0744d21b (b 0.94, cone 58.5), C-a76b61d0b046 (b 0.73, cone 34.7) and C-791ddbdead09 (b 1.10, cone 25.5) all sit where 2*b*cos(cone) is above about 0.98. Valid rows C-f9dcc6deb7b1 (0.92) and C-b9d89f4e803a (0.91) are below that.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Heat flux is set by nose radius and ballistic coefficient (stagnation heating ~ sqrt(rho/Rn)), so large D and large bluntness lower it. Bondline temperature follows the heat pulse duration and magnitude, so shallower gamma lengthens the pulse and raises it, while steeper gamma shortens it. Peak g rises with steeper gamma and higher ballistic coefficient. Mass fraction grows with shield area (~D^2 and cone length), so high cone angle and D of about 3 m is the best compromise. Cone angle must stay large enough for the chosen bluntness to avoid the sphere/shoulder overlap.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The flux and bondline models are fits to 10 valid points and partly rely on prior Allen-Eggers scaling, not on the data alone. The exact geometry-validity boundary is only bracketed (0.92 valid, 0.98 invalid). The mass-fraction limit and its dependence on cone angle and bluntness are extrapolated from about 8 points. The g dependence on D and cone angle is unknown, and g near -3.4 to -3.7 deg is a genuine coin flip.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-e948676086c1\",\"rationale\":\"Shrink the near-feasible C-e948676086c1 to D 3.1 to fix the mass fraction, and raise bluntness and cone angle to cut flux while staying geometry-valid (2b*cos = 0.73).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":310000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"First likely-feasible point; anchors the model near the g and mass boundaries.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e948676086c1\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.2, b 1.0, cone 68 at gamma -3.0 gives a slightly shallower entry for more g margin at low flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Candidate for the low-flux, low-temperature corner; mass fraction is near its limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-66547069c09c\",\"rationale\":\"Use C-66547069c09c's high-bluntness, high-cone shape at smaller D (3.0) and much shallower gamma (-3.4) to bring g under 12.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":304000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the steep end of the g-feasible range with high bluntness.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ddca85038195\",\"rationale\":\"C-ddca85038195 fails only g (12.9). Shallowing gamma to -3.3 and raising D to 2.8 and bluntness to 0.7 should put it inside 12 g.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.8,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.7,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":64.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":416000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Directly repairs the nearly feasible C-ddca85038195 and locates the g boundary.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ddca85038195\",\"rationale\":\"Larger D of 3.0 with moderate bluntness and gamma -2.8 gives comfortable g and mass margins.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.6,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":62.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":384000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Safe feasible point that maps the flux/temperature trade-off at mid gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b9d89f4e803a\",\"rationale\":\"C-b9d89f4e803a fails only bondline temperature (494 K) with small D and shallow gamma. Increase D to 2.6 and bluntness to 0.9 and steepen gamma to -2.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.6,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":371000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":426,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the shallow-gamma side of the trade-off with a smaller D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-66547069c09c\",\"rationale\":\"Push D to 3.25 with cone 70 (lowest mass) and bluntness 0.8 at gamma -3.0 to probe the mass limit at high D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.8,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":301000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the maximum feasible D; a success would dominate many other designs.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e948676086c1\",\"rationale\":\"Test near-maximum bluntness (1.25) at cone 69 (2b*cos = 0.90, just below the 0.919 that was valid) to see how much the flux drops.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.15,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":253000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Lowest-flux candidate; also refines the geometry validity boundary.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b9d89f4e803a\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow-side coverage of the front: D 2.8, b 0.8, cone 65, gamma -2.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.8,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.8,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":65.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":341000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":427,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether shallow gamma reduces flux enough to offset the higher bondline temperature.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b9d89f4e803a\",\"rationale\":\"Large D of 3.1 with high bluntness at gamma -2.0 gives the low-flux end of the front with wide g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":67.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":257000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":421,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends coverage toward low flux; the bondline rise at shallow gamma is uncertain.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-66547069c09c\",\"rationale\":\"Deliberately probe the g limit at gamma -3.7 with a good shape (D 3.1, b 1.0, cone 67); this predicts g just over 12.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":67.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":316000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g boundary; if feasible it gives the coolest bondline among feasible designs.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e948676086c1\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.3 and cone 70 with b 0.7 tests the mass-fraction limit with a moderately blunt nose.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.7,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":314000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Mass fraction is estimated at 0.96 of its limit here; the result will pin the mass boundary.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ddca85038195\",\"rationale\":\"Compare a low-bluntness nose (b 0.5) with #2 at similar D and cone to isolate the bluntness effect.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.5,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":397000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Separates the effect of bluntness on flux, bondline temperature and mass.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-62b9c4fe3119\",\"rationale\":\"C-62b9c4fe3119 fails only g at -7.6 deg. Keep its cone/bluntness family, enlarge D to 2.9, use cone 60 and gamma -3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.85,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":60.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":347000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests a moderate cone angle (60) for its effect on mass and g.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f9dcc6deb7b1\",\"rationale\":\"C-f9dcc6deb7b1 fails on mass and g. Reduce D to 3.0 and gamma to -3.2, keeping cone 48 to see how cone angle affects mass and g.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.65,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":48.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":383000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Isolates the effect of cone angle on mass fraction and g.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af897bb220d2\",\"rationale\":\"C-af897bb220d2 is a low-cone, low-bluntness design that failed on mass and g. Reduce D to 2.6, cone 30 and gamma -3.0 to see if it becomes feasible.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.6,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.4,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":30.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":595000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":434,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the low-cone family; the result is likely dominated but tests the flux and mass scaling.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-50d31993402b\",\"rationale\":\"Small-D check (2.2 m) of the scaling model at moderate bluntness and cone 64, gamma -3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.8,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":64.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":541000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":429,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Validates flux and temperature scaling with D at small size.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-66547069c09c\",\"rationale\":\"High-bluntness, max-cone design at D 2.9 and gamma -3.3 for a low-flux, low-temperature feasible point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":308000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Another sample of the high-bluntness region on the front with more mass margin.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ddca85038195\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-range point: D 3.05, b 0.75, cone 65, gamma -2.6, to fill the front between gamma -2.2 and -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.05,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.75,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":65.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":328000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the gamma gap along the front for hypervolume coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b424d80c454b\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.2 with cone 62 and b 0.9 at gamma -3.4 is a steeper, cooler variant of the high-D family.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":62.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":305000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the near-boundary g and mass corner (D 3.2, gamma -3.4) for a low bondline temperature.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":193259,"type":"result","duration_ms":244690,"uuid":"43681584-04c2-4ece-aa11-2daf5b7cf4a5","ttft_stream_ms":1516,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":1516,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
